From a83db054a01095ba2193bb439301ac3e7ae2d393 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:10:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: Preserve voltage stepping and failed request
 semantics

Keep intermediate voltage ranges valid while descending toward exact
consumer requests. Stop on balancing errors, restore request state on all
error paths, and reject same-range no-ops when a failed stepped change
left hardware outside the previous request. Accept converging final steps.

Add isolated public-API KUnit coverage for inherited voltage takeover,
short final steps, failure/retry behavior and stock OPP voltage pairs.

---
 Documentation/power/regulator/consumer.rst |   7 +
 drivers/regulator/Kconfig                  |   8 +
 drivers/regulator/Makefile                 |   1 +
 drivers/regulator/core-test.c              | 211 +++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/regulator/core.c                   |  47 +++--
 5 files changed, 257 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/regulator/core-test.c

diff --git a/Documentation/power/regulator/consumer.rst b/Documentation/power/regulator/consumer.rst
index c01675b25a90..9386f6a7a45f 100644
--- a/Documentation/power/regulator/consumer.rst
+++ b/Documentation/power/regulator/consumer.rst
@@ -111,6 +111,13 @@ when enabled, then the voltage changes instantly, otherwise the voltage
 configuration changes and the voltage is physically set when the regulator is
 next enabled.
 
+With a maximum voltage step constraint, an enabled regulator may need several
+intermediate settings before reaching the requested range. The call waits for
+each step's settling delay. If a step fails, the consumer's previous request
+is restored, but completed hardware steps are not automatically reversed.
+Consumers must handle the error before changing dependent clocks; an error
+does not mean that the physical voltage returned to its previous value.
+
 The regulators configured voltage output can be found by calling::
 
 	int regulator_get_voltage(regulator);
